 loss"], "rationale": "With no polls, ratings, or market prices to weigh, the forecast rests on Rhode Island's D+8 lean and its record of Democratic presidential margins, including double digits in recent cycles. An open race and signs of state-level Democratic frustration justify a wide error band but not a departure from the fundamentals.", "watch": "A national environment shifting toward Republicans, or early 2028 polling showing a much closer race, could move this toward tossup.", "confidence": "low", "notes": ["No expert ratings published yet; forecast rests on fundamentals and polls.", "New or vacant seat with no expert ratings; fundamentals only.", "No usable general-election polls; forecast rests on fundamentals and expert ratings."]}, "overview": "Rhode Island remains one of the most Democratic-leaning states in presidential voting, and the forecast starts there: an eight-point Democratic edge based purely on fundamentals. No general-election polls, expert ratings, or market prices are available, so the projection leans entirely on the state's partisan lean and its long record of backing Democrats for president, including by double digits in recent cycles.\n\nThe open nature of the contest, with no incumbent president on the ballot, adds uncertainty, as does evidence of local Democratic friction: the state's Democratic governor lost a 2026 primary amid voter anger over a bridge project. Still, presidential outcomes in Rhode Island have tracked national dynamics more than state ones, and the state has not voted Republican since 1988. The forecast keeps a wide error band and classifies the race as Lean Democratic with low confidence.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.8249, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.7734, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.7988, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.7688, "margin": 8.0}, {"date": "2026-09-27", "p_dem": 0.8114, "margin": 9.0}, {"date": "2026-09-28", "p_dem": 0.808